 "biases_checked": {
  "look-ahead (signal timing)": "Excluded structurally: the engine computes every signal from a closed-bar snapshot and fills entries at the NEXT bar's open.",
  "look-ahead (window boundary)": "Measured, not assumed. 2.47% of trades open inside a ranking window and close after it. Re-running with a strict rule (entry AND exit inside) moves the pooled out-of-sample figure by -0.00406R on average - the loose rule was mildly generous, so the conclusion is if anything understated.",
  "data-mining bias": "Quantified: 2,859,518 strategy evaluations, free_t 5.453, zero rows in any top 10 clear it.",
  "overfitting to the selection window": "Tested directly by disjoint thirds and by rolling walk-forward; the 1-month top 10 shares zero names with the 9-month top 10 in 6 of 6 cells because the two lists rank different populations.",
  "insufficient sample size": "The 20-trade floor admits 3-9 strategies in most 1-month 60m cells and 1-2 in the 240m thirds, so those 'top 10s' are the whole qualifying population. Flagged everywhere it occurs.",
  "clone inflation": "Collapsed on realised trades. Uncollapsed, MES 60m/274d reports 220 qualifiers and lists one TREND rule set four times inside its own top 10; collapsed it reports 116.",
  "unrealistic fills": "Every trade in this study comes from the library engine: stop wins when one bar holds both stop and target, gaps fill at the open. D35 (a limit credited with both extremes of one bar) lives in the ORB module's own fill code and cannot reach these results.",
  "understated costs and slippage": "Library CostModel applied to every trade; slippage widens with ATR percentile, thin books and news windows rather than being flat.",
  "survivorship": "None to correct: the population is generated, not selected from survivors. 82.1% of generated strategies never trade at all, which shrinks the effective search to ~495,000 and free_t to 5.15 - still uncleared.",
  "repainting indicators": "Structurally excluded by the closed-bar snapshot; not separately re-tested here.",
  "future-data leakage in the null": "The permutation null reassigns R only within (exit geometry x time block), so it preserves every block's pooled R and cannot import information from outside the block.",
  "nested-window double counting": "The central correction of this whole analysis. A strategy in all four top 10s is one observation seen four times; the nesting baseline is computed explicitly and the observed agreement does not exceed it."
 },
